<p><strong>AWS Web Application Firewall (AWS WAF)</strong></p>

<p>AWS Web Application Firewall (AWS WAF) is a web application firewall tha=
t helps protect web applications from attacks by allowing you to configure =
rules that allow, block, or monitor (count) web requests based on condition=
s that you define. These conditions include IP addresses, HTTP headers, HTT=
P body, URI strings, SQL injection, and cross-site scripting. You can use t=
he IP address based match rule to block specific geographies. The accuracy =
of the IP Address to country lookup database varies by Region. Based on rec=
ent tests, AWS mentions that the overall accuracy for the IP address to cou=
ntry mapping is 99.8%.</p>

